WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.360
What keeps a kinase off until cAMP arrives?

2
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.060
Protein kinase A reads cAMP.

3
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.940
At rest it is a complex of four subunits.

4
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.900
Two are catalytic subunits, and each is a complete kinase.

5
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.680
Two are regulatory subunits, which keep the catalytic ones off.

6
00:00:26.533 --> 00:00:32.553
The kinase phosphorylates a serine or threonine that lies close after a pair of

7
00:00:32.553 --> 00:00:33.913
arginines in its target.

8
00:00:35.073 --> 00:00:39.853
Each regulatory subunit carries a short stretch that looks like such a target.

9
00:00:40.753 --> 00:00:45.533
That stretch lies in the active site of the catalytic subunit, where a substrate

10
00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:46.533
would go.

11
00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:53.007
In type I regulatory subunits, the serine position holds a residue that cannot

12
00:00:53.007 --> 00:00:54.287
accept a phosphate.

13
00:00:55.007 --> 00:00:58.567
So the stretch fits, but it is never phosphorylated.

14
00:00:59.387 --> 00:01:01.247
It is called a pseudosubstrate.

15
00:01:02.227 --> 00:01:04.487
Think of a blank key left in a lock.

16
00:01:05.147 --> 00:01:09.607
It fits and will not turn, so no working key can get in.

17
00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:16.687
Each regulatory subunit has two binding sites for cAMP, four in the whole

18
00:01:16.687 --> 00:01:22.767
complex. When cAMP fills them, the subunit changes shape and lets go.

19
00:01:23.687 --> 00:01:28.127
In the classical model, the catalytic subunits come away free and begin

20
00:01:28.127 --> 00:01:29.527
phosphorylating targets.

21
00:01:30.427 --> 00:01:35.207
There is evidence that the kinase on an anchoring protein can act on nearby targets

22
00:01:35.207 --> 00:01:36.667
without fully coming apart.

23
00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.767
So the textbook picture may not hold everywhere.

24
00:01:40.747 --> 00:01:45.487
A kinase held shut by its own partner, until cAMP fills the sites.
